Subject: Re: [r-inla] RW(1) model
Message-ID: <_0jgIi5R6vI.-G_7BX5NAAAJ@r-inla-discussion-group.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <_0jgIi5R6vI.6UUjtYdGAAAJ@r-inla-discussion-group.groups.google.com>
References: <_0jgIi5R6vI.6UUjtYdGAAAJ@r-inla-discussion-group.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/r-inla-discussion-group/c/_0jgIi5R6vI/m/-G_7BX5NAAAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The two formulation describe the same model. The one in the book gives the full conditional distributions, I.e. when conditioning on both the past and future. The formulation you quote from the website is the sequential, timeseries, formulation, where conditioning is only on the past.

Finn

